-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Codebook Size**: Choosing $K > 4096$ yields minimal PSNR improvement but significantly increases storage [S1].
-*   **Pruning Parameters**: Incorrect $\beta_p$ or $\beta_k$ can lead to excessive quality loss or insufficient compression [S1].
-*   **Empty Codes**: During VQ update, some code vectors may not be assigned any voxels; the implementation keeps the previous vector [G].
-*   **Weight Quantization**: Aggressive weight quantization may degrade quality if not properly finetuned [S1].
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Codebook Size:** Choosing a codebook size larger than 4096 yields minimal PSNR improvement but significantly increases storage, making it inefficient [S1].
+*   **Pruning Parameters:** Incorrect tuning of $\beta_p$ and $\beta_k$ can lead to either excessive quality loss or insufficient compression. The default values (0.6 and 0.001) provide a balanced trade-off [S1].
+*   **Performance Drop:** Vector quantization alone causes a ~0.5 dB PSNR drop, which must be recovered via joint finetuning [S1].
